Reach the worker scope and start a worker without eval

A page whose content security policy leaves out 'unsafe-eval' refuses
JavaScript's eval, and wasm_thread evaluates code to reach the global scope,
to load a polyfill for module workers and, building its default worker
script, to find the address of the wasm-bindgen shim. The first spawn of a
thread so panics on such a page. js_sys::global() is the global scope
eval("self") named. Every browser with the Atomics.waitAsync that threads on
the web need also starts module workers, so the polyfill is left out. The
default worker script is built only for a builder given no worker script
URL, so a page that gives one never reaches the shim lookup.

